      "content": "It's a profound loss when your self-worth is tied so tightly to external achievements, and it's natural to feel like a piece of yourself has died. You are mourning the version of yourself you thought you were, and that grief is real and valid. Instead of trying to \"keep going\" as that old person, maybe you can start exploring what it means to be *you* without that title or success. The person you are now, even in this broken state, is still capable of change, even if it feels impossible right now.",
